@div proverb 26.a4

A.26.a4.30. aš₂ a₂ zig₃-ga bal-e di X [...] dumu-nitah e₂ ad-da-[na-ta] sar-ra niŋ₂-gig {d}nin-urta-[ke₄]
#lem: aš[curse]; a[arm]; zig[rise]; bala[turn]; di[speak]; X; X; dumunita[son]; e[house]; adda[father]; sar[run]; niŋgig[evil]; Ninurtak[1]DN
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.22,]{6.1.22: ll. 49-50}, @xref[t.6.2.3,t623.h74]{6.2.3: UET 6/2 259}, @xref[t.6.2.5,]{6.2.5: UM 29-16-519 Seg. B ll. 4-5}, @xref[t.6.2.5,t625.h17]{6.2.5: YBC 7351}, @xref[t.5.6.1,]{5.6.1: l. 50}} Violent cursing and chasing away a son from his father's house are abominations to @wDN{Ninurta}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a4.30

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.22: ll. 49-50, 6.2.3: UET 6/2 259, 6.2.5: UM 29-16-519 Seg. B ll. 4-5, 6.2.5: YBC 7351, 5.6.1: l. 50

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a5

A.26.a5.31. uš₇ dug₄-ga sahar nu-gi-[a] eme ak an-bar₇ an-dul₃ nu-ŋal₂-la niŋ₂-gig {d}utu-ke₄
#lem: uš[poison]; dug[speak]; sahar[soil]; gi[turn]; eme[tongue]; ak[do]; anbar[mid-day]; andul[shade]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; niŋgig[evil]; Utu[1]DN
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.03,t.6.1.03.8]{6.1.03.8}, @xref[t.6.2.1,]{6.2.1: Ni 4122 ll. 2-5}} To spit without covering it up with dust and to use the tongue at midday without protection are abominations to @wDN{Utu}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a5.31

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.03.8, 6.2.1: Ni 4122 ll. 2-5

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a6

A.26.a6.32. šu gi₄-gi₄ niŋ₂-gig {d}nin-urta-ke₄
#lem: šu[hand]; gi[turn]; niŋgig[evil]; Ninurtak[1]DN
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.11,t.6.1.11.66]{6.1.11.66}, @xref[t.6.2.5,]{6.2.5: UM 29-16-519 Seg. B l. 6}} To take revenge is an abomination to @wDN{Ninurta}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a6.32

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.11.66, 6.2.5: UM 29-16-519 Seg. B l. 6

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a7

A.26.a7.33. nu-dug₄-ga niŋ₂-gig {d}nin-urta-ke₄
#lem: dug[speak]; niŋgig[evil]; Ninurtak[1]DN
#tr.en: Refusing to talk is an abomination to @wDN{Ninurta}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a7.33

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a8

A.26.a8.34. niŋ₂ zu a-na-am₃ ga-ra-ad-da-be₂# niŋ₂ nu-zu a-na-am₃ lu₂-ki-inim ba-ab-e₃ niŋ₂-gig {d}utu-ke₄
#lem: niŋ[thing]; zu[know]; ana[what?]; dug[speak]; niŋ[thing]; zu[know]; ana[what?]; lukiʾinimak[witness]; e[leave]; niŋgig[evil]; Utu[1]DN
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.03,t.6.1.03.118]{6.1.03.118}} When a man comes forward as a witness, saying: @q{“Let me tell you what I know,”} but does not know the relevant information, it is an abomination to @wDN{Utu}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a8.34

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.03.118

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a9

A.26.a9.35. ki-ta kur₂ niŋ₂-gig {d}nin-urta-ke₄
#lem: ki[place]; kur[alienate]; niŋgig[evil]; Ninurtak[1]DN
#tr.en: To remove something from its proper place is an abomination to @wDN{Ninurta}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a9.35

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a10

A.26.a10.36. lu₂ {ŋiš}ma₂ dirig-ga lu₂ {ŋiš}ma₂ ru-ru-gu₂# niŋ₂ kab₂ di-dam niŋ₂-gig {d}suen-na-ke₄
#lem: lu[person]; ma[ship]; dirig[make more than]; lu[person]; ma[ship]; rugu[withstand]; niŋ[thing]; kab[test]; di[speak]; niŋgig[evil]; Suen[1]DN
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.03,t.6.1.03.170]{6.1.03.170}, @xref[t.6.1.25,t.6.1.25.13]{6.1.25.13}, @xref[t.6.2.5,]{6.2.5: BM 57994 Seg. A ll. 1-3}} When a man sailing downstream encounters a man whose boat is travelling upstream, to demand an inspection is an abomination to @wDN{Suen}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a10.36

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.03.170, 6.1.25.13, 6.2.5: BM 57994 Seg. A ll. 1-3

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a11

A.26.a11.37. {ŋiš}ma₂ niŋ₂-gen₆-na ni₂ ba-ab-dirig {d#}utu kar gen₆-na mu-un-na-ši-kiŋ₂-kiŋ₂
#lem: ma[ship]; niŋgina[truth]; ni[self]; dirig[make more than]; Utu[1]DN; kar[harbor]; gin[confirm]; kiŋ[seek]
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.01,t.6.1.01.83]{6.1.01.83}, @xref[t.6.2.3,t623.h7]{6.2.3: UET 6/2 302}, @xref[t.6.2.5,]{6.2.5: YBC 8713 ll. 4-5}} When a trustworthy boat sets sail, @wDN{Utu} seeks out a trustworthy harbour for it. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a11.37

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.01.83, 6.2.3: UET 6/2 302, 6.2.5: YBC 8713 ll. 4-5

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a12

A.26.a12.38. ni₂ teŋ₃-ŋe₂₆ nam-sag₉-ga in-tu-ud
#lem: ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]; namsag[pleasure]; utud[give birth (to)]
#tr.en: Fear of god creates good fortune. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a12.38

A.26.a12.39. er₂ nam-tag al-du₈-am₃#
#lem: er[tears]; namtaga[sin]; du[spread]
#tr.en: Lamentation absolves sin. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a12.39

A.26.a12.40. sizkur nam-til₃ ba-ab-tah-e
#lem: siškur[prayer]; namtil[life]; tah[add]
#tr.en: Offerings extend life. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26.a12.40

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.a13

A.26.a13.41. aš₂# dug₄-ga-ŋu₁₀ aš₂ nu-mu-un-[gi]
