D.26.d5.9. buru₁₄-ta gu₃-e lag nu-bur₁₂-re
#lem: buru[harvest]; gu[voice]; lag[clod (of earth)]; bur[tear out]
#tr.en: He who eats during the harvest is not removing clods. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d5.9

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d6

D.26.d6.10. gud sur₁₂-ra ab-sin₂-bi ab-sag₉-sag₉
#lem: gud[bull]; sur[threshing floor]; absin[furrow]; sag[good]
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.02,t.6.1.02.86]{6.1.02.86}, @xref[t.6.1.05,t.6.1.05.17]{6.1.05.17}} Furrows are pleasant to a threshing ox. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d6.10

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.02.86, 6.1.05.17

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d7

D.26.d7.11. ga-zi-in-bu lugal-ŋu₁₀ ur-saŋ mu-bi-im
#lem: gazinbu[pole]; lugal[king]; ursaŋ[warrior]; mu[name]
#tr.en: A stake, my lord; @q{“hero”} is its name. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d7.11

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d8

D.26.d8.12. ga-zi-in-bu su la₂-a nu₂-nu₂
#lem: gazinbu[pole]; su[flesh]; la[hang]; nud[lie down]
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.02,t.6.1.02.84]{6.1.02.84}} Salted meat lying on a stake. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d8.12

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.02.84

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d9

D.26.d9.13. gud gu₃ ra-ah lag-bi nu-bur₁₂-re
#lem: gud[bull]; gu[voice]; rah[beat]; lag[clod (of earth)]; bur[tear out]
#tr.en: The bellowing ox does not remove the clods. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d9.13

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d10

D.26.d10.14. gud sig₉-ga sahar-ra igi-bi zid₂ ak-a
#lem: gud[bull]; sig[put into]; sahar[soil]; igi[eye]; zid[flour]; ak[do]
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.02,t.6.1.02.90]{6.1.02.90}} The ox which has sunk into the ground -- in its own eyes it was still making flour. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d10.14

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.02.90

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d11

D.26.d11.15. {u₂}numun₂-bi {gi}en₃-bar sumun₂-bi niŋ₂ izi sag₃-ge niŋ₂ an-ta ed₂-de₃
#lem: numun[alfalfa grass]; enbar[reed]; sumun[old]; niŋ[thing]; izi[fire]; sag[strike]; niŋ[thing]; an[sky]; e[leave]
#tr.en: These rushes, these old reeds -- when set on fire, they come down from the sky. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d11.15

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d12

D.26.d12.16. id₂ niŋ₂ ŋal₂-la he₂-gid₂-i
#lem: id[river]; niŋ[thing]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; gid[long]
#tr.en: Let the river expand when there is something in it. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d12.16

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d13

D.26.d13.17. engar#-e a-šag₄ na-ab-daŋal-la
#lem: engar[farmer]; ašag[field]; daŋal[wide]
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.02,t.6.1.02.131]{6.1.02.131}} A farmer should not widen the field. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d13.17

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.02.131

D.26.d13.18. diŋir# lu₂-u₁₈-lu šag₄-gal-la-ni nam#-ba-ab-tah-e
#lem: diŋir[deity]; lulu[man]; šaggal[food]; tah[add]
#tr.en: A god (?) should not increase for mankind his food demands. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d13.18

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d14

D.26.d14.19. ŋi₆# 50-am₃ ud 50-am₃# ud# lul 55-[am₃]
#lem: ŋi[night]; n; ud[sun]; n; ud[sun]; lul[false]; n
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.14,t.6.1.14.62]{6.1.14.62}} The nights are fifty, the days are fifty; but the days (?) of lies (?) are fifty-five. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d14.19

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.14.62

@end proverb

@div proverb 26.d15

D.26.d15.20. [a]-da tuš! kur-šag₄-ga igi# [du₈]
#lem: a[water]; tuš[sit (down)]; kuršag[center of the mountains]; igi[eye]; du[spread]
#tr.en: @note{cf. @xref[t.6.1.02,t.6.1.02.149]{6.1.02.149}, @xref[t.6.1.11,t.6.1.11.69]{6.1.11.69}} Those who live near the water look into the mountains. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d15.20

#etcsl#cf cf. 6.1.02.149, 6.1.11.69

D.26.d15.21. [ni₂]-bi-še₃ [igi nu-du₈]
#lem: ni[self]; igi[eye]; du[spread]
#tr.en: They don't look in their own direction. 
#etcsl: line-id=D.26.d15.21

